    "created_at": "2026-07-06T09:51:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-07-06T09:51:42Z",
    "body": "The RegExp referenced by OP is not suggested syntax. The workaround provided by OP is to use a regex and looks for substrings that appear to be custom elements in the input variable `html` and then write them into the config.\n\nThis might work in some cases but is obviously brittle for two reasons\n* doesn't match the [valid custom element names](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/custom-elements.html#valid-custom-element-name) per spec.\n* will also match non-elements when a substring matches in comments, attributes etc.\n\nInstead, I'd use `Document.parseHTML()` combined with a [TreeWalker](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/TreeWalker) that can selectively handle the elements that the Sanitizer had to keep.\n\nBut I digress, we shouldn't talk about the workaround here, but how the use case from OP: Should we allow replacing custom elements with their children with our API? I think yes, that would be nice...\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
